<Folder id="Boca Raton Campus">
<name>📍 Boca Raton Campus</name>
<open>1</open>
<Folder id="CampusBuildingsB">
	<name>Campus Buildings</name>
	<Placemark id="AD10">
		<name>Administration Building, Kenneth R. Williams (AD-10)</name>
		<styleUrl>#__managed_style_0FBD889D9A4198B162F7</styleUrl>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10157585,26.37185862,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="HS26">
		<name>Alexander D. Henderson University School (HS-26H)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Alexander D. Henderson University School (ADHUS) is a cluster of buildings located off Florida Atlantic Boulevard. ADHUS is a public school functioning as a laboratory school located on the campus of FAU in Boca Raton. It serves as a site for student field experiences and provides an excellent opportunity for teacher trainees to work with highly qualified master teachers in a model school environment.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.096417,26.374676,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="GY38">
		<name>Arena (GY-38)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/38.jpg">

<p>Arena is situated on the west side of the Campus. The best way to get there is from the FAU main entrance on West University Drive and follow the signs. Convenient parking can be found in Lot 10 and Lot 14.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10938194588562,26.37207510321185,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FH11">
		<name>Athletic Field House Pool (FH-11)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/11.jpg">

<p>Completed in 1966, the Field House is located next to the swimming pool and the baseball stadium, just south of the Gymnasium. Parking is located in Lot 15.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10926735497181,26.37128604591781,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FW11A">
		<name>Athletic Field House West (FW-11A)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/11a.jpg">

<p>The Athletic Field House is located next to the pool off Volusia Street west of West Unniversity Drive. Parking is available in Lots 14 and 15.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.11007658687315,26.37158584565401,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="0A4A3A539D1A7CAFA573">
		<name>Atlantic Park Towers (AP-111)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/housing/images/tour/atlantic-park-towers.jpg">
<p>Atlantic Park Towers is a suite-style residence hall consisting of both double and single rooms for upper-division students. All suites feature a common entrance and either one or two bathroom facilities. Each bedroom is equipped with unlimited access to Ethernet connections. Students can access cable television via streaming.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10469268358133,26.36949620898904,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="PW62">
		<name>B.P.W Scholarship House (PW-62)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/62.jpg">

<p>BPW Scholarship House, was dedicated in 1996 with building costs of $360,000 provided by the Education Foundation of the Florida Federation of Business &amp; Professional Women&#39;s Clubs, Inc. It houses 16 students and one resident advisor. The BPW House is located behind the student apartments off Florida Atlantic Blvd.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09616584,26.36706259,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="KH25">
		<name>Barry Kaye Hall (KH-25)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/25.jpg">

<p>The recently renovated Barry Kaye Hall is located at the north end of the Breezeway and is off North University Drive. Convenient parking for students is located in Parking Garage I or Lot 7.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10335573082007,26.3731230246117,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="BB48">
		<name>Baseball Stadium (BB-48)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/48.jpg">

<p>The Baseball Stadium is located off of Volusia Street, west of West Unniversity Drive. Parking is available in Lot 15. The 1,200-seat lighted baseball stadium, with grass berms for spectators along the baselines, was built in 1990. It is home to FAU&#39;s intercollegiate baseball team and it hosts several amateur baseball tournaments each year.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10947227,26.37029181,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="BS12">
		<name>Behavioral Sciences (BS-12)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/12.jpg">

<p>The Behavioral Sciences Building was completed in 1967. The five-story facility is located off North University Drive and parking is in Lot 7 or 5. The building is also easily accessible at the north end of the Breezeway. Classrooms, laboratories and offices for the Departments of Behavioral, Biological Sciences and Psychology are located in this building.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10292875015527,26.37301094412412,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="CC45">
		<name>Bezos Academy Boca Raton (CC-45)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/45.jpg">

<p>Bezos Academy Boca Raton is a six classroom preschool located on FAU’s Boca Raton campus. Our goal is to nurture the potential in every child to become a creative leader, original thinker, and lifelong learner by increasing access to early childhood education in under-resourced communities.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09543091,26.37260838,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="BK76">
		<name>Bookstore (BK-76)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/76.jpg">

<p>The Florida Atlantic University Bookstore is located at the South end of the Breezeway across from the Cafeteria and near Starbucks. Purchase books, scantrons, snacks and other student needs.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10362110049392,26.37066024049998,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="CO69">
		<name>Campus Operations Building (CO-69)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/69.jpg">

<p>The Campus Operations building is located on the north end of campus on Florida Atlantic Boulevard. The Police department, University Architect and Vice President of Facilities, Facilities Planning, the Office of Space Utilization &amp; Analysis and EH&amp;S can be found here. Parking is available in front of the building.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09749680053356,26.37841029342773,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="AU31A">
		<name>Carole and Barry Kaye Auditorium (AU-31A)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/31a.jpg">

<p>The 2,400 seat Carole and Barry Kaye Performing Arts Auditorium, located in the Student Union, has performances ranging from comedians to opera. Many graduation ceremonies are held here as well. Convenient parking is located in Lots 15 and 16.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10569437488085,26.37028936450427,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="CM22">
		<name>Computer Center (CM-22)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/22.jpg">

<p>The Computer Center building is west of the Breezeway surrounded by the Library, Fleming Hall, and the Utilities building. It is easiest to park in Parking Garage I and walk east along the sidewalk adjacent to the College of Education.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10407759081467,26.37226049713624,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="CE31D">
		<name>Continuing Education Hall (CE-31D)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/31d.jpg">

<p>The Continuing Education Hall is on the west side of campus directly off of West University Drive. Parking is across the street in Lot 15. FAU serves the educational needs of retired and working adults through the Lifelong Learning Society and the Division of Open University and Continuing Education.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10704207828684,26.37059010449014,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SO44a">
		<name>College of Social Work and Criminal Justice (SO-44)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/44.jpg">

<p>The immense faculty expertise and strong community partnerships within our schools produce graduates who are prepared to make a difference. Our alumni enter the fields of social work and criminal justice fully trained to analyze, implement and evaluate criminal justice and social welfare policies, practices, and technologies; address discriminatory systems and processes; provide direct services to vulnerable and marginalized populations; and promote justice and equitable outcomes for individuals, families, and communities in South Florida and beyond.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10154366,26.37075321,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="AL09">
		<name>College of Arts &amp; Letters, Dorothy F. Schmidt (AL-9)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/9.jpg">

<p>Pursue your passion in the arts, humanities, or social sciences through 20 diverse undergraduate degree programs. Work closely with world-renowned faculty on inspiring research, pursue interdisciplinary interests through our certificate programs or explore the globe through robust study abroad options. See why our graduates are well-rounded and ready to succeed in a fast-changing economic world.</p>
<p>One of three buildings in the Dorothy F. Schmidt Center for Arts and Humanities, the 530-seat University Theatre is located in the Humanities Building. The theatre is used primarily for student theatre and musical performances and for special university ceremonies. There is easy access to this building off Indian River Street or East University Drive. Convenient parking is in Parking Garage II or Lot 25.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10192754472678,26.36933737392366,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="BU86">
		<name>College of Business in Phil Smith Hall (BU-86)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/86.jpg">
<p>College of Business offers executive education degrees and professional development for professionals who want to master their management skills and advance their careers in today's competitive marketplace. We also offer corporate and customized programs for organizations seeking to raise their employees to new levels of leadership and innovation.</p>
<p>Sharing space with Parking Garage III , the building is located on the north of North Unviversity Drive, just west of the FAU Stadium.
</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10474086000001,26.37316589,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SF103">
		<name>College of Business Executive Education (SF-103)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>College of Business offers executive education degrees and professional development for professionals who want to master their management skills and advance their careers in today's competitive marketplace. We also offer corporate and customized programs for organizations seeking to raise their employees to new levels of leadership and innovation.</p>
<p>Sharing space with Parking Garage III , the building is located on the north of North Unviversity Drive, just west of the FAU Stadium.
</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.103859,26.375213,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="ED47">
		<name>College of Education (ED-47)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/47.jpg">

<p>The College of Education is a four story building located at the intersection of North University Drive and West University Drive. It is easy to reach from the main entrance to campus off Glades Road or the Spanish River entrance. Convenient parking is in Parking Garage I or in Lots 6,7,8 and 9.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10587539237574,26.37319034797814,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="EE96a">
		<name>College of Engineering and Computer Science (EE-96)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/96.jpg">

<p>The FAU College of Engineering and Computer Science is internationally recognized for cutting edge research and education in the areas of Computer Science and Artificial intelligence (AI), Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Bioengineering, Civil, Environmental and Geomatics Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, and Ocean Engineering.</p>
<p>The building is located on the east side of the campus with parking in Lot 4, Lot 1 and Lot 27.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09838938999999,26.37283186,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="BC71">
		<name>College of Medicine, Charles E. Schmidt (BC-71)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/71.jpg">

<p>FAU’s Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is one of most recent LCME accredited medical schools in the U.S. The college was launched in 2010, when it became the 134th allopathic medical school in North America. The College matriculates 64 medical students each year and has been nationally recognized for its innovative curriculum. As a community-based medical school, the college's humanistic, high touch, high tech curriculum, coupled with its partnership with three independent health systems in Palm Beach County, offers students and patients a unique experience.</p>
<p>This five story building is located on the eastern end of East University Drive. The easiest way to reach the building is heading west on North University Drive from East University Drive. Convenient parking is in Lots 2 and 4</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10039568000001,26.37328123,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="NU84">
		<name>College of Nursing, Christine E. Lynn (NU-84)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/84.jpg">

<p>In thirty five years, the College has grown from six to approximately 1,400 students, expanded its programs to include baccalaureate through doctoral, moved from a division in the College of Social Science to a free-standing College, expanded offerings to three campuses, established eminent scholar chairs and professorships focused on advancing nursing knowledge, and created five major centers/institutes that provide the opportunity for research, education, and interdisciplinary collaboration.</p>
<p>The Christine E. Lynn College of Nursing is located on the east side of campus near the Social Science building. Student parking is available in Parking Garage II.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10050296999999,26.37086855,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SE43">
		<name>College of Science, Charles E. Schmidt (SE-43)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/43.jpg">

<p>The Charles E. Schmidt College of Science, named in honor of one of Florida Atlantic University's greatest benefactors, is the primary source of scientific research and education for more than three million people living and working in our service region of Southeast Florida. Through its academic departments and research centers, our College provides outstanding opportunities for both undergraduate and graduate science majors.</p>
<p>The Science Building is located off North University Drive near the College of Medicine building. There is convenient parking in Lots 4 and 5.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10166705,26.37326682,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="CU97">
		<name>Culture and Society Building (CU-97)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/97.jpg">

<p>The new Culture and Society building on Florida Atlantic University Boca Raton Campus is being designed to LEED (Leadership in Environmental and Engineering Design) Silver Certification. The new building is part of the College of Arts and Letters which contains the following buildings: Performing Arts Theater, Visual Arts Building, Arts and Humanities Building and the University Gallery. The goal of the building is to provide interior and exterior gathering places and be an anchor between the existing housing and main campus to the west and the College of Arts and Letters campus to the north and east. Parking is in Lot 23 to the south of the building.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.1018721435712,26.36821841242595,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="DS87">
		<name>DeSantis Pavilion (DS-87)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/87.jpg">

<p>The DeSantis Center Pavilion is a two story building located between the College of Business and Fleming West on North University Drive. Convenient parking is available in Parking Garage I and Lots 6 and 7. The Carl DeSantis Business and Economics Center for the Study and Development of the Motion Picture and Entertainment Industry was established in 1997 at Florida Atlantic University&#39;s College of Business. Its mission is to focus on the business and economics of the film industry by serving as an incubator for ideas, a forum for discussion, and a center for scholarly activity in the field.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.104444,26.373474,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="AH52">
		<name>Dorothy F. Schmidt Arts and Humanities (AH-52)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/52.jpg">

<p>Completed in 1966, the Humanities Building includes classrooms, offices, a 530-seat, acoustically perfect theatre, a black box theatre, a recital room and various music and art studios. The building is situated among a complex of three buildings that make up the Dorothy F. Schmidt Center for Arts and Humanities. There is easy access to this building off Indian River Street or Florida Atlantic Boulevard. Convenient parking is in Parking Garage II or Lot 25.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10126091413755,26.36969084959519,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="PA51">
		<name>Dorothy F. Schmidt Performing Arts Center (PA-51)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/51.jpg">

<p>A part of the three-building complex known as the Dorothy F. Schmidt Center for Arts and Humanities, the Schmidt Art Gallery is located in the Performing Arts Center. The state-of-the art gallery features several traveling shows during the academic year. There is easy access to this building off Indian River Street or Florida Atlantic Boulevard. Convenient parking is in Parking Garage II or Lot 25.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10141836934032,26.36896707039536,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="VA53">
		<name>Dorothy F. Schmidt Visual Arts Center (VA-53)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/53.jpg">

<p>One of three buildings in the Dorothy F. Schmidt Center for Arts and Humanities, the beautifully located Visual Arts Center fronts a tranquil lake, where the patio area provides an idyllic setting. The building includes studios for illustration, painting, sculpture and ceramics, and photography darkrooms. Also some classrooms and departmental offices for the Departments of Art, Communication, English, History, Languages and Linguistics, Music, Philosophy, and Theatre are located here. There is easy access to this building off Indian River Street or Florida Atlantic Boulevard. Convenient parking is in Parking Garage II or Lot 25.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10112100845343,26.36899421167846,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="PR75">
		<name>Eleanor R. Baldwin House (PR-75)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/75.jpg">

<p>The Eleanor Baldwin House is located off the 20th Street entrance to FAU. Philanthropist Eleanor R. Baldwin, a former high school teacher, is a longtime supporter of Florida Atlantic University. Her remarkable gift lead to the University funded construction of the University reception center and presidential residence that bears her name.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09517074,26.37086375,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="EE96">
		<name>Engineering East (EE-96)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/96.jpg">

<p>The new location for College of Engineering and Computer Science was designed to be the first Platinum LEED (Leadership in Environmental and Engineering Design) building in the State of Florida. The building is located on the east side of the campus with parking in Lot 4, Lot 1 and Lot 27.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09838938999999,26.37283186,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="EG36">
		<name>Engineering West (EG-36)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/36.jpg">

<p>Engineering West is located in the hart of the campus across from Library, off Dade Avenue. Student parking is located in Parking Garage I and there are few metered parking spaces in Lot 19 and 20.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10452628,26.37064747,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="EH85">
		<name>Environmental Health Support Facility (EH-85)</name>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09655924502275,26.37798471163298,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
