		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.095095,26.374348,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FS100">
		<name>FAU Stadium (FS-100)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/stadium.jpg">

<p>FAU Stadium is located on the north side of campus at the intersection of North University Dr. and FAU Blvd. The FAU Owls hosted the first home game of the 2011 season in the 30,000 seat stadium.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10220342252742,26.37548246049354,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FTF">
		<name>FAU Track &amp; Field</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>The Track &amp; Field Complex includes a state-of-the-art synthetic field and high performance track.  This is a shared use facility overseen by the Department of Campus Recreation and the Athletics Department.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.1085281,26.3736081,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FL24">
		<name>Fleming Hall (FL-24)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/24.jpg">

<p>Fleming Hall is a four story building located off the central area of North University Drive. It is easily accessible from all entrances to campus and convenient student parking can be found in Parking Garage I and Lot 7. There are a few metered parking spaces in front of the building.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10391249692776,26.37307090967557,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FW23">
		<name>Fleming West (FW-23)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/23.jpg">

<p>Fleming West is located betweeen Fleming Hall and the DeSantis Center Pavilion. Parking for students can be found in Parking Garage I and Lot 7.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10427619639951,26.37310102599798,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="LL31C">
		<name>Friedberg Lifelong Learning Center (LL-31C)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/31c.jpg">

<p>The Barry &amp; Florence Friedberg Lifelong Learning Center is located off West University Drive in building 31C. Parking can be found in Lot 15. FAU serves the educational needs of retired and working adults through the Lifelong Learning Society and the Division of Open University and Continuing Education. More than 16,000 older adults pursue intellectual stimulation, personal growth and cultural fellowship as members of FAU&#39;s Lifelong Learning Society, the largest such organization in the world. Thousands more area residents take courses, seminars and workshops offered through Open University and Continuing Education as degree- and non-degree seeking students.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10705089963862,26.37071931614477,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="GN73">
		<name>General Classroom North (GN-73)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/73.jpg">

<p>General Classroom North is a one story building situated between the Behavioral Science building and the Science and Engineering building located at the north end of campus. Student parking can be found in Lots 5 and 7. Staff parking is available in Lots 4 and 6.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10239862,26.3731767,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="GS02">
		<name>General Classroom South (GS-2)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/2.jpg">

<p>General Classroom South is located in the central part of campus on the Breezeway across the lawn from the Social Science building. Student parking is available in Parking Garage I.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10287002,26.3710596,0</coordinates>
