	<Placemark id="LO31B">
		<name>Live Oak Pavilion (LO-31B)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/31b.jpg">

<p>The Live Oak Pavilion is located across from Parking Garage I and can also be accessed through the University Center building. The building is a meeting and reception facility that consists of a single 6,000 sq ft room, which can be separated into four smaller rooms or any combination of adjoining rooms.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10587216042286,26.37081141199167,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="AZ79">
		<name>Louis &amp; Anne Green Memory &amp; Wellness Center (AZ-79)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/79.jpg">

<p>The Louis &amp; Anne Green Memory &amp; Wellness Center is located at the far north end of Florida Atlantic Boulevard, near the Palm Beach Community College. Parking is conveniently located in front of the building. There is a comprehensive array of innovative services and therapeutic programs specific to the needs of individuals with memory problems and their families.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.0972370782342,26.37943417647753,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FA94">
		<name>Marleen and Harold Forkas Alumni Center (FA-94)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/94.jpg">

<p>The Marleen and Harold Forkas Alumni Center provides a permanent venue on the Boca Raton campus for a variety of events and programs for alumni, students, faculty and staff, community and corporate partners. The building is located on the north side of the campus with parking adjacent to the building in Lots 6 and 7.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10348538838181,26.37422624911263,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="ME104">
		<name>Office Building One (ME-104)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>This five story building is located on the eastern end of East University Drive. The easiest way to reach the building is heading west on North University Drive from East University Drive. Convenient parking is in Lots 2 and 4</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10109300000001,26.373552,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="OD93">
		<name>Office Depot Center for Executive Education (OD-93)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/93.jpg">

<p>The state-of-the-art facility is a focal point for the University&#39;s broad spectrum of programs for the business community, including executive graduate programs, executive continuing education, extension programs and corporate training programs.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10505199000001,26.37339658,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="PH102">
		<name>Parliament Hall (PH-102)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<div>Parliament Hall (PAR) a suite-style residence hall consisting of both double and single rooms for freshmen. All suites feature a common entrance and two bathroom facilities. Each bedroom is equipped with unlimited access Ethernet connections and basic cable television service.<br></div>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09986574362998,26.36767935272138,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
