		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="RC91">
		<name>Recreation and Fitness Center (RC-91)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/91.jpg">

<p>The FAU Recreation and Fitness Center is the state-of-the-art facility where students, faculty, staff and alumni can meet, relax, workout and be engaged in FAU campus life. The building is located on the north side of the campus with parking conveniently located next to the building in Lot 4.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10289205274347,26.37423570592457,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="GR-66">
		<name>Research Greenhouse (GR-66)</name>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09495,26.377796,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="RS35A">
		<name>Research Support Facility (RS-35A)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>The Research Support Facility is located at the north end of the Breezeway next to the Behavioral Science building. Student parking is located in Lots 5 and 7.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09495,26.377796,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="AG39">
		<name>Ritter Art Gallery (AG-39)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/39.jpg">

<p>Enter FAU&#39;s main entrance on West University Drive. Follow signs to the Library/Ritter Gallery. Turn right at Volusia Avenue noticing 4 story parking structure on left. Continue straight until road turns to right. Turn into one of the first drives to left to enter parking lot 19 in front of Library. The Ritter Art Gallery is to the right of the Library on the 2nd floor. Metered parking in Lot 19 is available. Or you may purchase a temporary permit online or at the information booth during hours of operation. Please visit Parking and Transportation website for more information. After parking walk to area adjacent to entrance to Library. Look up to the east and notice a Ritter Art Gallery sign. You cannot enter the building where the sign is. You must walk under the breezeway past the Einstein&#39;s Cafe headed east until you intersect a longer breezeway. At the longer breezeway look and turn right to see signs and a stairway headed up stairs to the Ritter Art Gallery entrance.The facility is named for Mr. and Mrs. Roland Ritter, who funded a significant part of the construction cost of the gallery.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10356068999999,26.37149816,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="RC74">
		<name>Ropes Course Pavilion (RC-74)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/74.jpg">

<p>The Ropes Course Pavilion is located north of the Arena and the track. The best way to get there is go west on Volusia Street from West Universtiy Drive and turn north at the stop sign just past the gym. Continue straight past the Softball Stadium and park in Lot 12. The FAU Boca Campus opened its Ropes Challenge Course in March 2001. The L.I.F.T. program provides experiential workshops designed to build camaraderie and improve communication and problem-solving skills for fraternities, sororities, sports teams, clubs, classes, departments.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10885,26.37462212,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="TBT011">
		<name>ROTC (TB-T11)</name>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09520000000001,26.37838,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="LY03">
		<name>S. E. Wimberly Library (LY-3)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/3.jpg">

<p>The five-story S.E. Wimberly Library is located at the corner of Volusia Street and Dade Avenue. There are a few metered spaces in Lot 19. Additional parking is available in Parking Garage I.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10403047316294,26.37177864608432,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SC01">
		<name>Sanson Life Sciences (SC-1)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/1.jpg">

<p>Sanson Life Sciences is located toward the north end of the breezeway next to the Behavioral Science building. Parking is available in Parking Garage I as well as Lot 7.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10287941,26.37239691,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="PA51a">
		<name>Schmidt Center Gallery In Dorothy F. Schmidt Performing Arts Center (PA-51)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/51.jpg">

<p>A part of the three-building complex known as the Dorothy F. Schmidt Center for Arts and Humanities, the Schmidt Art Gallery is located in the Performing Arts Center. The state-of-the art gallery features several traveling shows during the academic year. There is easy access to this building off Indian River Street or Florida Atlantic Boulevard. Convenient parking is in Parking Garage II or Lot 25.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10141836934032,26.36896707039536,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SF107">
		<name>Schmidt Family Complex for Academic and Athletic Excellence  (SF-107)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="http://www.fau.edu/schmidt-complex/images/gateway.jpg">

<p>The Schmidt Family Complex for Academic and Athletic Excellence plays a central role in elevating Florida Atlantic University's (FAU) academic and athletic standing while helping student-athletes reach their greatest potential. The Complex is located next to FAU Stadium. In addition to a student-athlete academic and leadership center, the state-of-the-art facilities includes a strength and conditioning wellness center, sports medicine center, locker rooms, the FAU MBA Sport Management Program, a history and tradition hall, indoor training center and outdoor practice fields.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.103195,26.375267,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="0946ABCADF1A7C773F3E">
		<name>Sean Stein Pavilion in College of Business (BU-86)</name>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10455525432224,26.37320593640117,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SO44">
		<name>Social Science Building (SO-44)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/44.jpg">

<p>The Social Science building is located on the south side of the Administration building. The best parking is in Parking Garage II. The Social Science Building was completed in 1990. The structure features an open rotunda on the west side, and a 250-seat amphitheatre/lecture hall.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10154366,26.37075321,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SB68">
		<name>Softball Stadium (SB-68)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/68.jpg">

<p>The Softball Stadium is located in the NW corner of campus. The best way to get there is to turn west on Volusia Street off West University Drive and turn north just past the Arena. Convenient parking is available in Lots 12 and 14.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.11029048037543,26.37358703037888,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SP101">
		<name>Stadium Support Facility (SP-101)</name>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10341832394613,26.3769671334866,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="NU84a">
		<name>Stand Among Friends in C.E. Lynn College of Nursing (NU-84)</name>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10050296999999,26.37086855,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="CR31E">
		<name>Student Activities Center (CR-31E)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/31e.jpg">

<p>The Student Activities Center is located off West University Drive next to the Student Union. Convenient parking is available in Lots 16 and 15.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10647227983431,26.36986418744431,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SS08W">
		<name>Student Health Services (SS-8W)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/8w.jpg">

<p>Student Health Services is located at the far south end of the Breezeway. Take the stairs to the second floor above Starbucks.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10344600000001,26.370385,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SH46">
		<name>Student Housing Services (SH-46)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/46.jpg">

<p>Student Housing Services is located off Dade Avenue directly across from the Student Services Building. Parking is in Lot 16.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10494370995893,26.36878297709679,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SS08">
		<name>Student Services &amp; Food Court (SS-8)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/8.jpg">

<p>The Student Services Pavilion is next door to the bookstore and across the lawn from Starbucks. The Pavilion houses an ATM machine and has a small room that often has religious services.</p><p><b style="color:#CC0000;>Notice:</b> The second floor is currently under renovation. View our <a href="https://myfau.fau.edu/u/renovation">Student Services & Cafeteria (SS-8) Temporary Offices</a> page to find the temporary offices of the affected departments.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10301887999999,26.37032065,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SU80">
		<name>Student Support Services Facility (SU-80)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/80.jpg">

<p>The Student Support Services building is the first large building on the right as you enter the main entrance from Glades Road onto West University Drive. Convenient parking is located in Lot 16 near the building. Admissions, the Registrar&#39;s office, Traffic &amp; Parking, and other important departments are located in the Student Services building.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10582369010089,26.36912487746376,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="UN31">
		<name>Student Union (UN-31)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/31.jpg">

<p>The Student Union is located on the east side of West University Drive. The main entrance from Glades Road onto West University Drive is the best route to take. Convenient parking is located in front of the Student Union in Lot 16. For over thirty years, the Student Union has been the focus of activities, programs, services and facilities dedicated to enhancing our University community in an environment that embraces diversity. Whether you are a member of the campus community, alum, or a visitor, within these links you will find information on an array of student and community services, which will make your experience at FAU richer and more meaningful. The Student Union staff strives to adapt our programs and services to the ever changing needs of our students.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10596700000001,26.370306,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="PA51b">
		<name>Studio One Theatre in Dorothy F. Schmidt Performing Arts Center (PA-51)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/51.jpg">

<p>A part of the three-building complex known as the Dorothy F. Schmidt Center for Arts and Humanities, the Schmidt Art Gallery is located in the Performing Arts Center. The state-of-the art gallery features several traveling shows during the academic year. There is easy access to this building off Indian River Street or Florida Atlantic Boulevard. Convenient parking is in Parking Garage II or Lot 25.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10141836934032,26.36896707039536,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="07A84B280C4197ABC270">
		<name>Talon Hall (TH-112)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/housing/images/talon-hall-tour.jpg">
		Talon Hall is our seven-story residence hall on the Boca Raton Campus of Florida Atlantic University. Designed with comfort, community, and wellbeing in mind, Talon Hall will feature modern study areas to support academic success, along with spacious community kitchens. For relaxation and socializing, the building will offer a vibrant game room, a sundeck, and an outdoor pavilion complete with BBQ grills and a fire pit, perfect for gatherings under the South Florida sky. Talon Hall embodies the next generation of on-campus living at Florida Atlantic, where comfort meets community.]]></description>
		<LookAt>
			<longitude>-80.09834945006085</longitude>
			<latitude>26.36761546952175</latitude>
			<altitude>4.114886227729775</altitude>
			<heading>0</heading>
			<tilt>0</tilt>
			<gx:fovy>35</gx:fovy>
			<range>913.5418339013995</range>
			<altitudeMode>absolute</altitudeMode>
		</LookAt>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09814290355342,26.36759838699258,2.902230950071654</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="TE106">
		<name>Tech Runway (TE-106)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>At FAU Tech Runway we house, educate, mentor, and fund startups. Tech Runway is the “we” space on campus for innovators from ages 12+ hosting entrepreneurial workshops, boot camps, and major activities on behalf of the University. Tech Runway houses College of Medicine and Division of Research. Building is located in the Research and Development Park, by the Boca Raton Airport</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10028685633318,26.38355293529986,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="AC67">
		<name>Tom Oxley Athletic Center (AC-67)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/67.jpg">

<p>The Tom Oxley Athletic Center is located on the west side of the Arena and the pool. The best way to get there is to turn west on Volusia Street from West University Drive and continue straight until you see the Tom Oxley building on the left. Convenient parking in located in front of the center.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.11162718058542,26.37230676618755,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="AL09a">
		<name>University Theatre in Dorothy F. Schmidt College of Arts &amp; Letters (AL-9)</name>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10192754472678,26.36933737392366,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SA56">
		<name>University Village Apartments (SA-56)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/56.jpg">

<p>The University Village Student Apartments are located on the east side of Florida Atlantic Boulevard. Convenient parking for the residents is located on the east side of the apartments.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.09665663269445,26.36969278344841,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="UT05">
		<name>Utilities (UT-5)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/5.jpg">

<p>The Utilities building is located between Parking Garage I and the Computer Center. When the University opened in 1964, the Utilities Building was, of course, already in place. It has since been expanded and renovated to keep up with the energy management demands of a growing campus.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10515580768759,26.37240135506007,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="TC67B">
		<name>Wally Sanger Owl Club Center Ticket Office (TC-67B)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.fau.edu/mobile/images/buildings/67b.jpg">

<p>The Owl Club Center is housing the athletics marketing department, call center and ticket and development offices. Adjiacent to Tom Oxley Athletic Center, the Owl Club Center is a centralized location for athletics ticket sales, donation and marketing efforts.</p>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.11087775,26.37207971,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder id="DiningB">
	<name>Dining &amp; Retail</name>
	<visibility>0</visibility>
	<Placemark id="AtlanticDiningHall">
		<name>Atlantic Dining Hall</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>The Atlantic Dining Hall is Florida Atlantic University’s all-you-can-eat Dining Hall. A student favorite, the Atlantic Dining Hall is open to the entire FAU community and visitors. Our food philosophy is to “cook from scratch, menu responsibly and source sustainably”. In the dining hall, we use RGHb free milk and dairy, cage free eggs, hormone free poultry and source 80% of our vegetables and fruit within 100 miles of the campus. We also only use fair trade certified coffee and zero trans fat oils in our cooking. Students with dietary restrictions can also work with our team and chefs to ensure they get a balanced meal.</p> 
<ul>
<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10666782338629,26.37004695152025,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="brBoxoffice">
		<name>Box Office</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>The Box office is located inside the Student Union which is on the east side of Broward Avenue. The Box Office is the place to purchase tickets for on campus plays and events.</p>
	<ul>
		<li><B>Location:</b> UN-31</li>
		<li><a href="https://www.fauevents.com/" target="_blank">Website</a></li>
		<li><a href="tel:18005649539">1-800-564-9539</a></li>
	</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10598,26.370274,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="BuffaloWindWings">
		<name>Buffalo Wild Wings</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p style="color:red; font-weight:bold;">Coming Soon</p>
	  <p>Buffalo Wild Wings brings bold flavor and a lively atmosphere to FAU’s dining scene. With a menu full of saucy wings, burgers, and shareable snacks, it’s the ideal spot to catch the game, hang out with friends, or unwind after a long day. This new campus addition is sure to be a favorite for food, fun, and Falcon pride.</p> 
	  <ul>
			<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
		</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.103104,26.370258,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="Chickfila">
		<name>Chick-fil-A</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Enjoy one of the most popular and irresistible dining brands conveniently located adjacent to the Wimberly Library (along the Breezeway). Chick-fil-A offers the widely favored Chicken Sandwich, Waffle Fries, Market Salads, Grilled Chicken Sandwiches, and now serving breakfast.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.102559,26.370477,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="CopyCenter">
		<name>Copy Services</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="http://www.fau.edu/business-services/images/copy-services.jpg">

				<p>Copy Services offers an array of services, including copying and binding, graphic design, and in-office copier rentals and repair. There are numerous “Print for Pay” copiers located in various locations university-wide. </p>
				<ul>
					<li><B>Location:</b> SS-8W </li>
					<li><a href="http://www.fau.edu/business-services/retail-services/copy-services.php/" target="_blank">Website</a></li>
					<li><a href="tel:15612970996">561-297-3508</a></li>
				</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.1035723,26.370523,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="DunkinDonuts">
		<name>Dunkin Donuts</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Everything we do is about you. From chefs who create exciting new flavors, to crew members who know exactly how you want your drink—we prioritize what you need to get you on your way. We strive to keep you at your best, and we remain loyal to you, your tastes and your time. That’s what America runs on.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10377800000001,26.371743,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="JimmyJohns">
		<name>Jimmy John&apos;s</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p style="color:red; font-weight:bold;">Coming Soon</p>
		<p>Jimmy John's is now serving up its famously fast and fresh sandwiches right on campus. Whether you're rushing between classes or looking for a laid-back lunch spot, this new location offers a variety of hand-crafted subs made with quality ingredients and speedy service that fits the student lifestyle. It’s the perfect grab-and-go option for busy Owls.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.103103,26.370518,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="esports">
		<name>eSports Arena and  Gaming</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="http://www.fau.edu/studentunion/images/1000x500-studentunion16.jpg">
		 
<p>Located in the Student Union,  the high-tech environment features 40 to 45 top-of-the-line gaming PCs, as well as consoles and wall monitors for spectators to follow the action. Each station is be furnished with a comfortable gaming chair and desk.
</p>                      <ul>
						<li><a href="https://www.fau.edu/studentunion/eSports/" target="_blank">Website</a></li>
				   </ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10644622535455,26.37005563388708,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="FAUClub">
		<name>The FAU Club</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>FAU’s premier dining location on campus, open to all campus faculty and staff. Our Chef prepared menu is small batched and prepared fresh. The location features a fresh salad bar, desserts and rotating lunch menu.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://dineoncampus.com/fau/fau-club-weekly-menu" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.097874,26.37277,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="Katora">
		<name>Katora | Food Truck</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Authentic Indian meals inspired by traditional home cooking, made with wholesome ingredients and bold regional flavors 🍛✨</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10314099999999,26.370703,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="brNewEra">
		<name>New Era Barber Shop</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>New Era Barbershop is ready to pamper you! This unique shop is open to students, faculty, staff and guests, and offers a wide range of services. </p>
	<ul>
		<li><B>Location:</b> SS-8W</li>
		<li><a href="http://www.fau.edu/business-services/barbershop/" target="_blank">Website</a></li>
		<li><a href="tel:15612970996">561-297-0996</a></li>
	</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10326999999999,26.370504,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="OuttakesBreezeway">
		<name>The Market - Breezeway Food Court</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Our state-of-the-art convenience market, located in the Breezeway Food Court, offers a full line of grab and go gourmet sandwiches, soups, salads, hot and cold beverages, groceries, sundries and baked goods.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10279800000001,26.37052,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="OuttakesSU">
		<name>The Market - Student Union</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Our state-of-the-art convenience market, located in the Student Union, offers a full line of grab and go gourmet sandwiches, soups, salads, hot and cold beverages, groceries, sundries and baked goods.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.105681,26.370094,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="Pizza">
		<name>Manhattan Joe&apos;s Pizza</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Manhattan Joe's Pizzeria is a fast, fresh Italian concept that will quickly become your favorite. Manhattan Joe's pizza is as authentic as it gets. Using only the finest ingredients, each pizza is hand tossed and baked to perfection. Our salads and Italian sandwiches are made to order. Enjoy our menu items in the Breezeway foodcourt. </p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.102941,26.370421,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="PandaExpress">
		<name>Panda Express</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Bringing people together to share joy has been our family’s inspiration since opening the first Panda Express in 1983 in Glendale, California. As we continue to open restaurants from coast to coast and around the world, the bold flavors of Chinese  cuisine inspire our cooking, while our extended family of guests and associates remains at the heart of what we do. Welcome to our family’ Chinese Kitchen.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.103072,26.370406,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="Starbucks">
		<name>Starbucks</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Starbucks is a hub for the whole campus. Starbucks is passionate about ethically sourcing the finest coffee beans, roasting them with great care and improving the lives of people who grow them. In our store you can find the latest deals, promotions and menu items.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.103319,26.370302,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="Subway">
		<name>Subway</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Subway is the world's largest submarine sandwich chain and is the leading choice for people seeking quick, nutritious meals that the whole family can enjoy. Subway serves fresh, delicious, made-to-order sandwiches. Our location offers special deals for the FAU community</p> 
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.101207,26.375334,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="sushi">
		<name>Sushi Maki</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Sushi Maki opened in 2000, and we’ve been on a roll (pun intended) spreading the joy of what great sushi should be; delicious, responsibly sourced ingredients and tasty combinations — an experience you’ll want to have again and again.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.102953,26.370234,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="TacosAlCarbon">
		<name>Tacos Al Carbon</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Tacos Al Carbon began its journey December 5, 1998 in a small five by seven concession trailer. Our goal was to provide our customers with great authentic Mexican food at a great price. Taco by taco we worked hard to open our first restaurant.</p>
<ul>
		<li><a href="https://new.dineoncampus.com/fau" target="_blank">Hours &amp; Menus</a></li>
</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.102813,26.37026,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder id="StuServicesB">
	<name>Student Services</name>
	<visibility>0</visibility>
	<Placemark id="brUndergrad">
		<name>Admissions (Undergraduate)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<ul>
		<li><B>Location:</b> SU-80, First Floor</li>
		<li><a href="http://www.fau.edu/admissions/" target="_blank">Website</a></li>
		<li><a href="mailto:admissions@fau.edu">admissions@fau.edu</a></li>
		<li><a href="tel:15612973040">561-297-3040</a></li>
	</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.10547699999999,26.369594,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="brGradCollege">
		<name>Admissions (Graduate)</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<ul>
