<Folder id="nonfauBuildingsJ">
	<name>Non FAU Buildings</name>
	<visibility>0</visibility>
	<Placemark id="MAXPLANCK">
		<name>Max Planck Florida Institute for Neuroscience</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mpfi.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/1-Contact_header_MPFIbuilding_9170_3300-1000x755.jpg">

	<p>Part of the prestigious Max Planck Society based in Germany, MPFI is its first and only institute in North America. Situated in the growing biosciences cluster in scenic Palm Beach County in South Florida, MPFI provides a vibrant, collaborative environment where scientists are provided generous ongoing support to conduct high impact research at the cutting edge.</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://mpfi.org/" target="_blank">Website</a></li>
		<li><a href="tel:15619729000">561-972-9000</a></li>
	</ul>]]></description>
		<Point>
			<coordinates>-80.114873,26.88392,0</coordinates>
		</Point>
	</Placemark>
	<Placemark id="SCRIPPSa">
		<name>Scripps Research, Florida</name>
		<description><![CDATA[<img src="https://www.scripps.edu/_files/images/campuses/florida/600x380_jupiter_campus.jpg">

	<p>The scenic Jupiter, Florida campus of Scripps Research encompasses three buildings on 30 lush acres within Palm Beach County.s innovation corridor, between Interstate 95 and the Atlantic Ocean. Here dozens of principal investigators work with their laboratory members to understand disease and develop effective treatments. Regularly honored by the National Institutes of Health and prestigious disease foundations for their discoveries, this elite team continues to pioneer innovations in translational research. They are complemented by a 500-member group of executives, staff scientists, graduate students and administrative assistants.</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://www.scripps.edu/campuses/florida/" target="_blank">Website</a></li>
		<li><a href="tel:15612282000">561-228-2000</a></li>
	</ul>]]></description>
